/*
:name: mod_cycle_unresolvable
:type: error
:error: literal, compile-time constant
:help: resolvable to one
*/

// A landing cycle must be a literal or a compile-time constant. The lambda's
// own input `d` is a runtime value, so `@[d]` cannot resolve to a single
// landing cycle. (This test used to read a file-scope `mut` made unresolvable
// by a conditional write; ruling 2026-09-27 #4 makes ANY enclosing runtime
// binding unreadable from a lambda -- errors/nested_lambda_signature_const --
// so the unresolvable name is now the lambda's own input.)
mod f(a:U8, d:U8) -> (x:U8@[d]) { x = a }   // locate_error_here
